acceptance_criteria: "Every read command that supports more than one output shape emits an omission receipt naming the withheld field groups or sections, and for each one the exact flag that restores it; A shape that withholds nothing emits an explicit empty receipt, so a complete payload and a missing receipt can never look alike; The receipt is derived from the same declared contract that drives the shapes, so adding a field group makes it appear in the receipt with no per-command edit, proven by a fixture group no command declares today; The receipt is bounded and constant per command: a test asserts its size does not scale with the number of rows or the size of the corpus; pm get at brief depth names children, claim_state and linked as withheld, and pm activity in compact mode names the provenance group as withheld, because both are silent today and both are the cases that produced wrong conclusions; Row omission and field omission use one vocabulary: the receipt keys read consistently against the existing has_more, applied_limit and next_cursor keys rather than introducing a parallel naming scheme"
